# Coding Conventions

Naming, imports, style, and file focus for the frontend.

## Naming

- Files: `snake_case.dart`.
- Classes, enums, typedefs, extensions: `PascalCase`.
- Variables, methods, parameters, providers: `camelCase`.
- Private members: `_privateName`.

## Imports

- Use package imports across folders; relative only within a small folder tree.
- No circular imports; order Dart SDK → Flutter → packages → project.

## Style

- Use `const` constructors where possible; keep widgets small with no business logic.
- Use typed models, not maps, for app data.
- Must not hard-code route strings, user-facing text, colors, spacing, or repeated formatting; use design tokens ([`design-system.mdc`](./design-system.mdc)).
- Localize all user-facing text via ARB keys; must not define `_XxxText` copy classes.
- Use `human_friendly_id` in routes and user-visible identifiers, not raw database IDs.
- Reuse shared components from `frontend/lib/shared/` before creating feature widgets.
- Enforce RBAC+ABAC visibility for menus, components, and actions ([`permissions.mdc`](./permissions.mdc)).
- Keep `*_workspace_page.dart` compositional; extract widgets near ~800 lines.

## File focus

| Suffix | Owns |
|---|---|
| `*_page.dart` | page composition |
| `*_controller.dart` | user actions, presentation state |
| `*_state.dart` | UI state shape |
| `*_repository.dart` | domain contract |
| `*_repository_impl.dart` | data coordination |
| `*_dto.dart` | API shape (`snake_case` JSON) |
| `*_mapper.dart` | explicit conversion |

